perature in {value}.","detail":"An engine that stays cold burns more fuel, wears faster and can hold back boost. Short winter trips can trigger this without a fault.","causes":["Thermostat stuck open","Coolant temperature sensor reading low","Very short trips in cold weather"]},{"id":"fuel_trim_idle","title":"Fuel mixture at idle","alert":"Running lean at idle","category":"Fuel mixture","when":"rpm > 500 && rpm < 1100 && speed < 3 && coolant_temp > 70","needs":"idling with a warm engine","value":"fuel_trim_b1","stat":"mean","settle_s":3,"min_time_s":30,"unit":"%","dec":1,"levels":[{"severity":"warning","gt":15},{"severity":"advisory","gt":9},{"severity":"warning","lt":-15},{"severity":"advisory","lt":-9}],"summary":"The engine is adding {value} fuel at idle to keep the mixture right.","ok":"Idle fuel trim is {value}.","detail":"Extra fuel at idle that fades as load rises points to air getting in after the air meter. Left alone it leads to rough idle and lean codes (P0171).","causes":["Vacuum or intake leak (hoses, PCV valve, intake manifold gasket)","Leaking brake booster line","Dirty or failing air mass / pressure sensor","Exhaust leak ahead of the oxygen sensor"],"low":{"alert":"Running rich at idle","summary":"Idle fuel trim is {value}: the engine is taking fuel out to compensate.","detail":"The engine is getting more fuel than it asks for at idle.","causes":["Leaking injector","Purge valve stuck open","Fuel in the oil from many short trips","Air sensor reading high"]}},{"id":"fuel_trim_load","title":"Fuel mixture under load","alert":"Running lean under load","category":"Fuel mixture","when":"engine_load > 60 && rpm > 2000 && coolant_temp > 70","needs":"accelerating with a warm engine","value":"fuel_trim_b1","stat":"mean","settle_s":1,"min_time_s":12,"unit":"%","dec":1,"levels":[{"severity":"critical","gt":22},{"severity":"warning","gt":14},{"severity":"advisory","gt":9},{"severity":"warning","lt":-15},{"severity":"advisory","lt":-10}],"summary":"The engine is adding {value} fuel under load.","ok":"Fuel trim under load is {value}.","detail":"Needing extra fuel when working hard means fuel delivery is not keeping up, or the engine is under-reading its air. Lean under load is the dangerous direction for a turbo engine.","causes":["Weak fuel pump or clogged filter","High-pressure pump or its cam follower wearing","Air mass sensor under-reading","Boost leak after the air meter"],"low":{"alert":"Running rich under load","summary":"Fuel trim under load is {value}: the engine is taking fuel out to compensate.","detail":"The engine is getting more fuel than it asks for when working hard.","causes":["Leaking or over-delivering injector","Fuel pressure too high","Boost leak on engines that measure air by flow","Air sensor reading high"]}},{"id":"fuel_trim_bank_split","title":"Fuel mixture, bank to bank","alert":"Cylinder banks disagree on fuel","category":"Fuel mixture","when":"coolant_temp > 70 && rpm > 500","needs":"driving with a warm engine","value":"abs(fuel_trim_b1 - fuel_trim_b2)","stat":"mean","min_time_s":120,"unit":"%","dec":1,"levels":[{"severity":"warning","gt":12},{"severity":"advisory","gt":7}],"summary":"The two cylinder banks differ by {value} in fuel trim.","ok":"Both banks agree within {value}.","detail":"A fault on one side only: one bank is compensating for something the other is not.","causes":["Intake leak on one bank","Injector or oxygen sensor on one bank","Exhaust leak on one bank"]},{"id":"boost_under_target","title":"Boost pressure","alert":"Boost below target","category":"Boost","when":"accel_pedal > 60 && rpm > 2000 && boost_target > baro + 35","needs":"hard acceleration above 2000 rpm","value":"boost_target - boost_actual","stat":"p90","settle_s":2,"min_time_s":6,"unit":"kPa","dec":1,"levels":[{"severity":"critical","gt":35},{"severity":"warning","gt":20},{"severity":"advisory","gt":12}],"summary":"Boost fell {value} short of what the engine asked for under hard acceleration.","ok":"Boost reaches its target (largest shortfall {value}).","detail":"The turbo is not delivering the pressure requested. This often shows up here before a P0299 code or limp mode.","causes":["Boost leak (charge pipes, couplers, intercooler)","Diverter (recirculation) valve leaking","Wastegate actuator or its control","PCV valve failure","Worn turbocharger"]},{"id":"boost_over_target","title":"Boost overshoot","alert":"Boost above target","category":"Boost","when":"accel_pedal > 60 && rpm > 2000 && boost_target > baro + 35","needs":"hard acceleration above 2000 rpm","value":"max(boost_actual - boost_target, 0)","stat":"p90","settle_s":2,"min_time_s":6,"unit":"kPa","dec":1,"levels":[{"severity":"critical","gt":45},{"severity":"warning","gt":30}],"summary":"Boost overshot its target by {value}.","ok":"Boost stays at its target (largest overshoot {value}).","detail":"More boost than requested stresses the engine and can trigger an overboost code (P0234).","causes":["Wastegate sticking closed","Boost control solenoid or its vacuum lines","Boost pressure sensor"]},{"id":"charge_temp_rise","title":"Intake air temperature","alert":"Intake air much hotter than outside","category":"Boost","when":"speed > 50 && rpm > 1000","needs":"driving at road speed","value":"intake_air_temp - ambient_temp","stat":"p90","min_time_s":120,"unit":"Δ°C","dec":0,"levels":[{"severity":"warning","gt":45},{"severity":"advisory","gt":32}],"summary":"Intake air ran {value} above outside temperature while moving.","ok":"Intake air stays within {value} of outside temperature while moving.","detail":"Hot intake air costs power and makes the engine pull ignition timing.","causes":["Intercooler blocked or its airflow obstructed","Heat soak after stop-and-go driving","Intake temperature sensor fault"]},{"id":"charging_low","title":"Charging voltage","alert":"Charging voltage low","category":"Electrical","when":"rpm > 1000","needs":"the engine above idle speed","value":"vbat","stat":"p90","min_time_s":120,"unit":"V","dec":2,"levels":[{"severity":"critical","lt":12.6},{"severity":"warning","lt":13.1}],"summary":"System voltage only reached {value} with the engine running.","ok":"The charging system reaches {value}.","detail":"The alternator is not lifting system voltage. Smart charging can hold voltage low for a while, so this looks at the upper end of what was seen.","causes":["Alternator or its regulator","Drive belt slipping","Battery at end of life","Poor ground or battery terminal connection"]},{"id":"charging_high","title":"Over-voltage","alert":"Charging voltage too high","category":"Electrical","when":"rpm > 1000","needs":"the engine above idle speed","value":"vbat","stat":"p95","min_time_s":120,"unit":"V","dec":2,"levels":[{"severity":"critical","gt":16},{"severity":"warning","gt":15.4}],"summary":"System voltage reached {value}.","ok":"No over-voltage (peak {value}).","detail":"Over-voltage cooks the battery and can damage electronics. Cars that recover energy while slowing down briefly charge near 15 V on purpose, so the limit sits above that.","causes":["Voltage regulator fault","Battery sensor fault"]},{"id":"oil_overheat","title":"Oil temperature","alert":"Oil running hot","category":"Lubrication","when":"rpm > 400","needs":"the engine running","value":"oil_temp","stat":"max","min_time_s":60,"unit":"°C","dec":0,"levels":[{"severity":"critical","gt":140},{"severity":"warning","gt":130}],"summary":"Oil reached {value}.","ok":"Oil peaked at {value}.","detail":"Oil this hot thins out and breaks down quickly.","causes":["Sustained high load or towing","Low oil level","Oil cooler or its coolant supply"]},{"id":"catalyst_overheat","title":"Catalyst temperature","alert":"Catalyst running hot","category":"Exhaust","when":"rpm > 400","needs":"the engine running","value":"cat_temp","stat":"max","min_time_s":60,"unit":"°C","dec":0,"levels":[{"severity":"critical","gt":980},{"severity":"warning","gt":920}],"summary":"The catalyst reached {value}.","ok":"Catalyst peaked at {value}.","detail":"Very high catalyst temperature usually means unburned fuel is reaching it.","causes":["Misfires","Rich mixture","Sustained full-load driving"]},{"id":"codes_cleared_recently","title":"Self-test history","alert":"Trouble codes were cleared recently","category":"Diagnostics","when":"rpm > 400","needs":"the engine running","value":"clr_dist","stat":"last","min_time_s":5,"unit":"km","dec":0,"levels":[{"severity":"advisory","lt":80}],"summary":"Codes were cleared {value} ago; the car has not finished re-checking itself.","ok":"{value} since codes were last cleared.","detail":"After a clear (or a battery disconnect) the self-tests start over. A fault can be present without a code until they have run again.","causes":["Battery was disconnected or replaced","Codes were erased with a scan tool"]},{"id":"knock_retard","title":"Knock control","alert":"Engine pulling ignition timing","category":"Ignition","when":"accel_pedal > 45 && rpm > 1800 && coolant_temp > 70","needs":"firm acceleration with a warm engine","value":"knock_retard_worst","stat":"p95","settle_s":0.5,"min_time_s":6,"unit":"°","dec":1,"levels":[{"severity":"critical","gt":8},{"severity":"warning","gt":5},{"severity":"advisory","gt":3.5}],"summary":"Under load the engine pulled up to {value} of timing to stop knock.","ok":"Knock control is quiet (up to {value} under load).","detail":"A little knock retard is normal. Consistently large corrections mean the engine is protecting itself and giving up power.","causes":["Low-octane or poor fuel","Carbon build-up on intake valves and pistons","Hot intake air (see intake air temperature)","Worn spark plugs or wrong heat range","Oil dilution or low oil quality"]},{"id":"knock_one_cylinder","title":"Knock, cylinder to cylinder","alert":"One cylinder knocks more than the others","category":"Ignition","when":"accel_pedal > 45 && rpm > 1800 && coolant_temp > 70","needs":"firm acceleration with a warm engine","value":"knock_retard_spread","stat":"p90","settle_s":0.5,"min_time_s":6,"unit":"°","dec":1,"levels":[{"severity":"warning","gt":4.5},{"severity":"advisory","gt":3}],"summary":"One cylinder is pulling {value} more timing than the quietest one.","ok":"All cylinders knock-correct alike (spread {value}).","detail":"When a single cylinder stands out, the cause is local to it.","causes":["Spark plug or ignition coil on that cylinder","Injector spray pattern or flow","Carbon deposits in that cylinder"]},{"id":"misfires","title":"Misfires","alert":"Misfires counted","category":"Ignition","when":"rpm > 500","needs":"the engine running","value":"misfire_total","stat":"max","min_time_s":60,"unit":"","dec":0,"levels":[{"severity":"critical","gt":60},{"severity":"warning","gt":12},{"severity":"advisory","gt":2}],"summary":"The engine counted up to {value} misfires.","ok":"No misfires counted.","detail":"Misfires send unburned fuel into the catalyst. A flashing check-engine light means stop driving hard now.","causes":["Ignition coil or spark plug","Injector","Intake leak","Carbon build-up on intake valves","Low compression"]},{"id":"chain_stretch_intake","title":"Timing chain (intake cam)","alert":"Timing chain stretch","category":"Valve timing","when":"rpm > 500","needs":"the engine running","value":"abs(cam_adapt_in)","stat":"last","min_time_s":5,"unit":"°","dec":1,"levels":[{"severity":"critical","gt":5.5},{"severity":"warning","gt":4},{"severity":"advisory","gt":3}],"summary":"The engine has shifted intake cam timing by {value} to make up for chain wear.","ok":"Intake cam adaptation is {value}, inside the limit.","detail":"The engine computer learns how far the camshaft has drifted from the crankshaft as the chain and tensioner wear. Volkswagen's replacement limit is about 4° on these engines, and correlation faults (P0016) appear near 6°. Watch the trend week to week: a chain does not un-stretch.","causes":["Timing chain elongation","Chain tensioner","Worn guides or sprockets"]},{"id":"chain_stretch_exhaust","title":"Timing chain (exhaust cam)","alert":"Timing chain stretch, exhaust side","category":"Valve timing","when":"rpm > 500","needs":"the engine running","value":"abs(cam_adapt_ex)","stat":"last","min_time_s":5,"unit":"°","dec":1,"levels":[{"severity":"warning","gt":5},{"severity":"advisory","gt":3.5}],"summary":"Exhaust cam timing has been shifted by {value}.","ok":"Exhaust cam adaptation is {value}.","detail":"The same learning as the intake side, for the exhaust camshaft.","causes":["Timing chain elongation","Chain tensioner"]},{"id":"cam_tracking","title":"Variable valve timing","alert":"Cam timing not following its target","category":"Valve timing","when":"rpm > 1500 && coolant_temp > 70","needs":"driving above 1500 rpm with a warm engine","value":"abs(cam_in_actual - cam_in_target)","stat":"p95","min_time_s":60,"unit":"°","dec":1,"levels":[{"severity":"warning","gt":8},{"severity":"advisory","gt":5}],"summary":"The intake cam lagged its target by up to {value}.","ok":"The intake cam follows its target (within {value}).","detail":"The variable valve timing adjuster is slow or not reaching position.","causes":["Cam adjuster solenoid (magnet)","Low or dirty oil","Cam adjuster itself"]},{"id":"rail_pressure_low","title":"High-pressure fuel","alert":"Fuel rail pressure below target","category":"Fuel delivery","when":"rpm > 1500 && engine_load > 40 && rail_pressure_target > 3000","needs":"accelerating above 1500 rpm","value":"(rail_pressure_target - rail_pressure) / rail_pressure_target * 100","stat":"p90","settle_s":1.5,"min_time_s":10,"unit":"%","dec":0,"levels":[{"severity":"critical","gt":25},{"severity":"warning","gt":15},{"severity":"advisory","gt":9}],"summary":"Fuel rail pressure fell {value} short of target under load.","ok":"Fuel rail pressure follows its target (within {value}).","detail":"The high-pressure fuel system is not keeping up with demand.","causes":["High-pressure fuel pump","Low-side pump or filter not feeding it","Fuel pressure regulator valve","Leaking injector"]},{"id":"lp_fuel_low","title":"Low-pressure fuel","alert":"Low-side fuel pressure low","category":"Fuel delivery","when":"rpm > 600","needs":"the engine running","value":"lp_fuel_pressure","stat":"min","min_time_s":60,"unit":"kPa","dec":0,"levels":[{"severity":"critical","lt":250},{"severity":"warning","lt":330}],"summary":"Low-side fuel pressure dropped to {value}.","ok":"Low-side fuel pressure stays above {value}.","detail":"The in-tank pump feeds the high-pressure pump. If it sags, the engine leans out under load.","causes":["In-tank fuel pump","Fuel pump control module","Clogged fuel filter"]}],"id":"vw-tiguan-mk2","name":"Volkswagen Tiguan (2018+, 2.0 TSI)"}